  "critical_branch_justification": "The graph has no terms below degree3. Substitute b=V*t in H_b and divide by V^2. Its constant quadratic in t has two distinct roots because lambda2 is nonzero. The analytic implicit-function theorem gives two critical branches with distinct slopes. Their images are h=c_plus*V^3+O(V^4) and h=c_minus*V^3+O(V^4), with (c\u2212mu3)^2+gamma=0 and gamma nonzero. Thus the two local branch images have contact order3. The displayed degree6 equation is only their leading weighted equation, with weights wt(V)=1, wt(h)=3.",
